# fixedbugs, defect d-lane-win-longname-2, 2026-11-27, lane win-paths
# (M-rebel-library step 212h).
#
# SYMPTOM: a correct program whose root is named in 220 letters was refused
# by `heroes run`, `test` and `build` with no `-o` on Windows, from a folder
# of the CI's 18 characters: *cannot write build/<16>/<module>.exe: its whole
# path ... is 266 characters, past the 259 Windows takes in a path*, exit 2,
# where the same program with `-o` built. The binary's home is the
# compiler's choice, `build/<16>/`, and it named the binary by the module
# whole, so a path the compiler chose grew with a name the program chose.
#
# FIX: the binary's own name in its home holds at most 48 bytes: the
# module's whole up to that, and past it its first 31, `-` and a digest of
# the whole (`selfhost/cli/link_output.hero`'s `home_name`). This root's
# name takes 196 characters, 195 of them letters, so the `run` form's
# `heroes run` with no `-o` builds and runs it under that shorter name on
# every platform. It cannot show the refusal from the CI's folder: the form
# first builds every case with `-o build/harness-<pid>/binaries/<case>.exe`,
# a path of the harness's own five characters longer than the compiler's
# home, so a name long enough to pass the limit there is refused at the
# harness's `-o` first. The roots of 200 to 240 letters at folders of 18 and
# 44 characters were run by hand on the Windows box, before and after.
function main()
    print("run with no -o, its name of 196 characters held to 48 in its binary")
